# Borderlands SHiFT Code Aggregator - Environment Variables

# ===========================================
# Twitter API (GitHub Actions)
# ===========================================
# Twitter fetching is handled by GitHub Actions, not the browser.
# Add TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN as a GitHub repository secret, NOT here.
#
# To set up:
# 1. Go to your GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
# 2. Click "New repository secret"
# 3. Name: TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN
# 4. Value: Your Twitter API Bearer Token
#
# The workflow runs daily and commits new codes automatically.

# ===========================================
# Reddit Scraping (GitHub Actions)
# ===========================================
# Reddit scraping uses the public .json endpoints — no API keys needed.
# The workflow runs daily at 9 AM UTC and commits new codes automatically.
# Subreddits scraped: r/Borderlands4, r/Borderlands, r/borderlands3, r/Borderlandsshiftcodes

# ===========================================
# Local Testing (Optional)
# ===========================================
# Only needed if you want to run the fetch scripts locally.
# NOTE: this is read by the Node scripts in scripts/, NOT by the browser app.
# Never give it a VITE_ prefix — Vite inlines VITE_* values into the public
# bundle, which would publish your token. In CI it comes from Actions secrets.
# TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN=your_bearer_token_here

# ===========================================
# Remote Data Source (Optional)
# ===========================================
# Public URL to fetch SHiFT codes from a remote JSON endpoint.
# Use this for centralized data updates without redeploying.
# Setting it at build time switches the app from embedded data to remote
# fetching; leave it empty to use the codes embedded in shiftCodes.ts.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE_URL=
